<title>USA: DenAmerica Q1 net loss narrows.</title>
<headline>DenAmerica Q1 net loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>SCOTTSDALE, Ariz. 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Quarter Ended</p>
<p>							  4/2/97    3/27/96</p>
<p>							 (13 wks)  (13 wks)</p>
<p> Restaurant sales				  $ 76,114  $ 20,161</p>
<p>Loss before minority interest, income taxes</p>
<p>   and extraordinary item			 (1,090)   (1,038)</p>
<p> Minority interest in joint ventures	    (109)	 (2)</p>
<p>Loss before income taxes and extraordinary</p>
<p>   item						   (981)   (1,036)</p>
<p> Income tax benefit				   (392)     (359)</p>
<p> Loss before extraordinary item		   (589)     (677)</p>
<p> Extraordinary item					 -     (497)</p>
<p> Net loss						 (589)   (1,174)</p>
<p> Preferred stock dividend and accretion	     -     (149)</p>
<p> Net loss applicable to common shareholders   (589)   (1,323)</p>
<p> Net loss per share				  (0.04)    (0.19)</p>
<p> Weighted average common shares outstanding  13,424     6,938</p>
<p>		 (In thousands, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE:  DenAmerica Corp said that as a result of its March 1996 merger with American Family Restaurants, and its July 1996 acquisition of Black-eyed Pea, year-over-year results for the first quarter are not comparable. The historical company financial statements are those of Denwest Restaurant Corp, and as a result of the reverse acquisition, historical American Family Restaurants financials are not presented.</p>
<p>Net loss for the first quarter of 1996 included an extraordinary loss of $497,000.</p>
<p>The change in the average shares outstanding reflects the March 1996 merger of Denwest Restaurant Corp and American Family Restaurants, to form DenAmerica.</p>
